    "drying": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "ink",
        "layout": "boxes",
        "numbered": true,
        "eyebrow": "The other end",
        "heading": "The ride home starts where the ride in finished.",
        "lede": "<p>Almost every product in this category is designed around the outbound journey. The commute has two halves and only one of them has a radiator at the end.</p>",
        "link_label": "How to wash them properly",
        "link_url": "/pages/care-and-washing",
        "mirror": false
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "A shoe does not dry in eight hours",
            "body": "<p>Especially not under a desk, in a building with the heating on a timer. Overshoes protect the shoe on the way in; they do not dry it by five o'clock.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "A sock can be swapped",
            "body": "<p>A second pair in a bag weighs almost nothing and means the evening ride starts dry even if the shoe does not. This is the practical reason commuters buy two pairs, not a sales argument.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Wash cool, air dry overnight",
            "body": "<p>They will be ready for the morning. They will not be ready in two hours, and they must never go on a radiator — direct heat is what ends a membrane.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
        "i2",
        "i3"
      ]
    },
    "fit": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "paper",
        "layout": "cards",
        "numbered": false,
        "eyebrow": "Fit",
        "heading": "Check the shoe before you order.",
        "lede": "<p>Cycling shoes are built with far less volume than a walking boot, so this matters more here than on any other page.</p>",
        "link_label": "The size bands in centimetres",
        "link_url": "/pages/size-guide",
        "mirror": false
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Roughly a cushioned training sock",
            "body": "<p>If your shoes are already snug in a thin summer sock, they will be tight in these. Winter shoes and commuting shoes usually have room. Race-fit road shoes often do not.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Take the larger band if you are between two",
            "body": "<p>A tight sock in a tight shoe creates a pressure point across the toes that you will notice at about mile four.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Some people size the shoe up for winter",
            "body": "<p>If you already run a half size up in winter shoes, these fit that space exactly. If you do not, try them in the shoe before committing to a long ride.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
        "i2",
        "i3"
      ]
    },
    "problem": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "paper",
        "layout": "steps",
        "numbered": false,
        "eyebrow": "The problem",
        "heading": "Upwards, mostly.",
        "lede": "<p>Riding in the rain is not really a rain problem. It is a spray problem, and spray behaves differently.</p>",
        "mirror": false
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Off the front wheel, onto the ankle",
            "body": "<p>The front wheel throws a continuous fan of water backwards onto the shoe and the ankle. That is where an overshoe is open, and it is where an overshoe ends.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Standing water, at speed",
            "body": "<p>A puddle taken at twenty miles an hour goes into the shoe through the vents in a way that rain simply does not.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "The road is dirtier than the rain",
            "body": "<p>Road spray carries grit and oil. It stains, it abrades and it is why cycling kit wears out faster than walking kit.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i4": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "And then there is nowhere to dry it",
            "body": "<p>A soaked cycling shoe does not dry under an office desk in eight hours. The evening ride starts wet regardless of the forecast.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
        "i2",
        "i3",
        "i4"
      ]
    }
